Sval: the most specific domain policy entry decides whether a page runs script

SvalJavascript keeps a rule per site and per host in the domain policy's
super lists. PolicyAllowsScript read only the lists that flip
javascript.enabled, so a host's allow could not beat its site's block while
script is on, nor a host's block its site's allow while it is off. The
lookup takes the entry of the most specific name in either direction
(SvalScriptPolicy.cpp).

